# Task 5 — DocGenStateMachine: Seed + Compose + checker (spec 40, design §4)

Executor: architect (Claude). D-rung: D3 — full live run on seeded dev tenant.

## What shipped

- `services/qms-generation/` — NEW service:
  - `grouping.ts` — GEN-3 by construction (shared → one merged section across
    in-scope standards; forked/standard_only → per-standard, section key
    `<hk>#<standard>`; exclusions → `na_justified` carrying justification).
  - `gap.ts` — GAP decided in CODE before any model call; REGISTER_TABLE_MAP
    maps register sources to real tables; unbuilt modules (aspects, hazards,
    competence, …) are null → definitionally empty → always gap, $0. Unknown
    source scheme fails toward GAP, never invention.
  - `checker.ts` — deterministic post-pass: assertion coverage (≥1 factRef,
    all resolve), house style (no shall/bullets/placeholders/second-person,
    org-as-subject), CLR-3 banned-fragment screen (curated list — official
    standards not in repo by licensing; "shall" check catches the dominant
    class).
  - `facts.ts` — citable facts ONLY from tenant data (profile + register
    rows); absent fields produce NO fact, so invention fails the checker.
  - `appsync-publish.ts` — FIRST real Lambda→AppSync IAM publisher in the
    codebase (SigV4 'appsync', NodeSha256 reused from the AOSS client);
    best-effort by design (audit trail is the durable record).
  - `seed-sections.ts` / `compose-section.ts` / `finalize-manual.ts` (stub:
    terminal status semantics + run_complete; m1 writes = Task 6).
- `qms.ts` — `generateImsManual` (M1-role-gated): pinned profile version, run
  row commits BEFORE StartExecution; StartExecution failure marks the run
  'failed' + throws GENERATION_UNAVAILABLE (never a running row with no
  execution). `regenerateSection` DEFERRED to Task 6/7 wave (needs
  FinalizeManual's m1 writes) — reported, not omitted.
- Infra: DocGenStateMachine (AiStack, Standard, 2h timeout, Map
  MaxConcurrency 4) named DETERMINISTICALLY `cumplify-docgen-<env>` — QmsFn
  (ApiStack) constructs the ARN by name; no CFN cycle (AiStack already
  depends on ApiStack). GeneralBucket newly exported from DataStack.
- detailTypes registered SAME COMMIT (the BC-5 lesson):
  Generation.SectionComposed / SectionFailed / RunCompleted (+ events.md).
- Tests: grouping matrix (8), GAP decision table + checker fixtures incl.
  the mandated unmapped-sentence-FAILS case (17), handler tests — idempotent
  re-seed SQL pins, GAP-path-ZERO-invoker-calls, pending-guard skip (4),
  infra pins — deterministic SM name, MaxConcurrency 4, compose role has
  lambda:InvokeFunction and ZERO bedrock:* actions (one door) (3).

## Live defects found & fixed during deploy/readback (both in-lane)

1. **Cross-stack export ordering**: first AiStack deploy rolled back — the new
   GeneralBucket export didn't exist until DataStack deployed. Fix: deploy
   DataStack (outputs only) first. Lesson: new cross-stack refs = producer
   stack deploys first.
2. **Wrong CMK for the app-role secret**: granted dbSecretKey (master-secret
   key); the app-role secret is encrypted with the dynamodb/secrets CMK
   (api-stack.ts AppRoleSecret) → KMS denial at first SeedSections run.
   Fixed grant + WHY comment; the failed execution then became the GEN-5
   resume test (below).

